---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StudioSample from '../../components/StudioSample.astro';
import StudioLab from '../../components/StudioLab.astro';
import '../../styles/studio.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Studio Lab | Make a little something | David Blumenau" description="A small, local creative workshop. Make an animated social tile and download your own image or four-second clip.">
 <main id="main" class="studio-page">
 <section class="studio-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="studio-return" href="/#small-work-title"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> More small tools</a><div class="studio-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Studio Lab / Borrow the tools</p><h1>Make a little<br /><em>something.</em></h1></div><div class="studio-hero-copy"><p>Borrow a small piece of Kitforge: set some words in moving ink, find a frame you like, and take a print home.</p><a class="text-link studio-start" href="#studio-controls">Edit the words <Icon name="arrow-down" /></a><span class="studio-local"><span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="dot" /></span> Made here, in your browser.</span></div></div></section>
 <div class="wrap"><StudioLab /><StudioSample /></div>
 <section class="studio-note wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">The machinery behind the ink</p><h2>One composition.<br /><em>Every frame.</em></h2></div><div><p>Kitforge started as a practical way to make event announcements. Its drawing function takes a document and a time, then paints a frame. The live preview and your downloaded print use that same function.</p><p>This workshop adapts the real Kitforge renderer, text fitting and looping shader backgrounds. It adds local portfolio typefaces and three arrangements. Photos, uploads and accounts stay outside this small exercise.</p><details><summary>Sources, credits and browser support</summary><p>Adapted from David’s Kitforge revision <code>809d559</code>. Amber, Teal and Forest are three original Kitforge presets powered by Paper Shaders 0.0.80. Preview and exports use the same four-second baked frame sequence, with a dissolve that closes the loop.</p><p>PNG and JPG use your browser’s canvas encoder. MP4 uses Kitforge’s Chromium-gated native WebCodecs H.264 path and mp4-muxer 5.2.2. If a compatible encoder is unavailable, you can download a still. A device without WebGL2 receives a gradient still.</p><p>Paper Shaders is Apache-2.0: <a href="/notices/studio/paper-notice.txt">attribution</a>, <a href="/notices/studio/paper-license.txt">license</a>. mp4-muxer is MIT: <a href="/notices/studio/mp4-muxer-license.txt">license</a>. DM Sans and Fraunces are bundled locally with this portfolio.</p></details><a class="text-link" href="/#small-work-title">See Kitforge in use <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></div></section>
 </main>
</BaseLayout>
